These factors include assessing:
(i) whether the offence affects the society at large;
(ii) the probability of the crime being repeated;
(iii) the potential of the convict to commit crimes in future;
(iv) if any fruitful purpose is being served by keeping the convict in prison; and (v) the socio-economic condition of the convict's family.
Ganesh Sah vs The State Of Bihar Through The Chief ... on 10 November, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120476085/
